// Dungeons (GDD, section 11): Rune Golem (Wind), Wyvern Nest (Fire), Bone King's Crypt (Dark), Drowned
// Sanctum (Water) and the Cracked Forge (Light). Each one is mostly its element, so the team that beats it is
// the one with the advantage (Fire, Water, Light, Wind, Dark). Enemies go past 6-star level 40, up to 60, and
// "scale" multiplies their HP and Attack (the calibration of each floor).
// The Golem, the Wyvern, the Crypt and the Sanctum are specialization content: their bosses (Data/enemies.json) have a
// mechanic a generic team can't overpower, and only a team built for that boss beats them. Floor 1 shows the
// mechanic, floor 2 makes the element count, floor 3 asks for a real composition, floor 4 for runes (the
// sweet spot: 5 stars, skills maxed and the right rune sets dominate it) and floor 5 for everything at once:
// 6 stars, Awakening, 6-star runes and a team made for the boss, about 20 days of play to get there for the
// Golem. Even a strong team without the tools fails it (dotnet run --project Tests -- --dungeons).
// The Forge still follows the reward: floor 1 is about stage 15 (where 2-3 star runes are the
// norm), floor 2 stage 30, floor 3 the end of the Campaign, floor 4 6-star level 40 with 5-star runes +12,
// floor 5 the same with 6-star runes +15.
// Each victory costs the floor's Mana ("mana"); a defeat costs nothing.
// Each Dungeon has its own team. "firstClearGold" is the Gold of the first victory on the floor. Every
// victory drops the loot, by the floor's chances in % (the same table in every Dungeon): "grades" are the
// rune's stars and "rarities" the rune's rarity, or the grade of each Grindstone / Enchanted Gem the Forge
// drops ("toolCount" of them). Rune Dungeons drop only their four sets. "scrollChance" is the chance in %
// of a victory also dropping a Mystic Scroll, "coreChance" of it dropping an Infusion Core (the same: 1%, 2% and 3%
// on floors 3, 4 and 5). Milestones of the
// first victory on each floor (Core/Progression/Milestones): "firstClearCores" Infusion Cores, a Legendary Scroll
// on floor 4 ("firstClearLegendary") and a Light and Dark Scroll on floor 5 ("firstClearLightDark"). "unlockStage" is the Campaign stage that opens the Dungeon.
